 "caption": "In 2019 an amateur team from Miami knocked a pro club out of the U.S. Open Cup. ⚽\n\nFlorida Soccer Soldiers, founded in 2018 and playing in the UPSL, won four qualifiers (9–1 on aggregate), beat Miami FC 2–1 with an 87th-minute winner, then beat Charlotte Independence, a Division II pro club, on penalties. Their run ended 1–0 against North Carolina FC.\n\nThe pyramid: MLS (Div I) → USL Championship (Div II) → USL League One (Div III) → amateur leagues like UPSL, NPSL and USL League Two. Amateur clubs can qualify for the Open Cup.\n\nYour Sunday team could be next. Find your club on Cancha, link in bio.\nSources: TheCup.us, FBref, Wikipedia.\n#miamisoccer #usopencup #upsl #adultsoccer",
